# Chapter data invariants

Full format spec: `docs/chapter-dsl.md`. Read it before editing any `.txt`.

## Never break line numbering

In `src/data/*.txt`, **the line number is the chapter number**. Empty lines are
real chapters with no outgoing paths (e.g. line 266 of
`T02-la-confrerie-de-nuada.txt`), and the parser keeps them on purpose.

- Never delete, insert, reorder or sort lines to "clean up" a file.
- To blank a chapter, leave the line empty. To add one, append at the end.
- Do not strip trailing whitespace in a way that removes blank lines.

## There is no build step

The app parses the `.txt` files at runtime: `services/books.ts` imports them
with `?raw`, `services/chapterDsl.ts` parses them, `services/bookGraph.ts` turns
them into nodes and edges, and `services/graphLayout.ts` hands that to elkjs.
Editing a `.txt` shows up on the next reload, with nothing to regenerate and no
generated artifact to commit.

## Adding a book

Add the `.txt` to `src/data/`, then add an entry to the `books` array in
`src/services/books.ts` (`id`, `title`, `category`, `chapterToSkip`, `content`)
and its id to the `BookId` union. `BookVisualizer` builds its select straight
from that array, so nothing else needs touching.

## Token semantics live in one place

`src/services/chapterType.ts` is the only registry of DSL keys. Each entry
carries the legend `label`, the `shape`, the `className` the stylesheet paints,
and an `extractPaths` telling which arguments are really outgoing paths. Node
colours are in `src/components/StoryDisplayer/storyDisplayer.css`, keyed by the
same class names.

## Notes

- An unknown `KEY-` token is parsed as an `unknown` token and contributes no
  path, rather than failing the render.
- `chapterToSkip` silently drops incoming paths to the listed chapters. So does
  a path pointing at a chapter the book does not have.
- Layout is cached per book for the session, because the tabs remount page
  components on every switch and laying out ~350 chapters takes about a second.
